
Maze App (v3.0.0)
=================

USAGE
  maze <command> [options]
  maze -h | --help

COMMANDS
  generate    Generate and print a maze (no solving)
  solve       Generate or load a maze, then solve and print the path
  save        Generate a maze and save it to a JSON file
  load        Load a maze from a JSON file and print it

GENERATION OPTIONS  (generate / solve / save)
  --width   INT       Maze width in columns            (default: 20)
  --height  INT       Maze height in rows              (default: 10)
  --seed    INT       Random seed for reproducibility  (default: random)
  --start   ROW,COL   Start coordinate                 (default: 0,0)
  --end     ROW,COL   End coordinate                   (default: last cell)

SOLVE OPTIONS
  --algorithm NAME    Solver: bfs | dfs | astar        (default: bfs)
  --file    FILE      Load maze from FILE instead of generating

SAVE OPTIONS
  --output  FILE      Output file path                 (default: maze.json)

LOAD OPTIONS
  --file    FILE      Path to a saved maze JSON file   (required)

EXAMPLES
  # Generate and print a 30×15 maze with a fixed seed
  maze generate --width 30 --height 15 --seed 42

  # Solve the same maze using A* (custom start/end)
  maze solve --width 30 --height 15 --seed 42 \
      --start 0,0 --end 14,29 --algorithm astar

  # Save a maze to file, then load and solve it with DFS
  maze save --width 20 --height 10 --seed 7 --output my_maze.json
  maze load --file my_maze.json
  maze solve --file my_maze.json --algorithm dfs
